  "answer_text": "No, the authors' conclusions do not agree with their reported results. The abstract and conclusion of the study state that retrieval augmentation makes the generated answers less accurate [S009, 0-1270] and that grounding the generator in retrieved documents yields less accurate answers [S009, 3633-3932]. However, the reported results indicate that the RAG pipeline achieved a higher fact-level accuracy (0.74) than the parametric-only model (0.68) on the main benchmark, NewsTruthQA, and a similar or slightly lower accuracy on LawFactQA (0.71 vs 0.72), which contradicts the conclusion that retrieval augmentation yields less accurate answers [S009, 1271-2418].",
